WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.880
To measure a speed, you would normally
time something over a known distance.

2
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:09.210
But waves can move far too fast to
time with a stopwatch in your hand.

3
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.380
So put the stopwatch away.

4
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.880
Send a wave at a known
frequency towards a hard wall,

5
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.140
and let it meet its own reflection.

6
00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:20.010
The two waves form a stationary wave.

7
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:24.070
How can that measure the wave's
speed, without timing anything?

8
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.650
In this mission, you'll set up
stationary waves on the lab bench,

9
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.080
at a frequency you know,
and take real readings.

10
00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.750
Then you'll turn those readings
into the speed of the wave.

11
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.270
Your mission: find out how stationary
waves can measure a wave's speed,

12
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:40.440
without a timer.
